[PHASE2] Security understanding extracted analysis:
To prevent writing beyond the bounds of an array with 16 elements when using `memset`, we need to ensure that the `count` does not exceed the available space from `begin_index`. Here's how you can modify the function:
```c
void set_values_in_arr(long long* values, int begin_index, int count) {
    if (values == NULL || begin_index < 0 || count <= 0)
        return;
    // Calculate maximum possible elements to avoid overflow
    int max_possible = 16 - begin_index;
    if (max_possible <= 0) {
        return; // No space available
    }
    if (count > max_possible) {
        count = max_possible; // Adjust count to fit within bounds
    }
    memset(values + begin_index, 0, count * sizeof(long long));
}
